WEBVTT

00:00:00.317 --> 00:00:03.198
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Law and order, 1

00:00:03.746 --> 00:00:05.327
Prison sentences

00:00:06.289 --> 00:00:08.672
Ideally, the fear of punishment

00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:12.229
should discourage people from committing a crime in the first place.

00:00:12.514 --> 00:00:18.582
However, studies show that, while short to medium prison sentences may be a deterrent,

00:00:18.813 --> 00:00:24.210
longer sentences have only a limited effect. In deciding the sentence,

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:29.419
the court will take into consideration things like the seriousness of the offence,

00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:33.311
whether the defendant pleads guilty or not guilty,

00:00:33.581 --> 00:00:37.944
and whether their criminal record shows that they are a serial offender.

00:00:38.786 --> 00:00:45.516
The judge will also consider any mitigating circumstances, e.g. diminished responsibility,

00:00:45.888 --> 00:00:51.315
i.e. the person’s mental state means that they are not fully responsible for a crime.

00:00:51.942 --> 00:00:56.336
<v><b>Sentences can be non- custodial:</b></v> a fine is paid,

00:00:56.399 --> 00:01:00.738
or community service, such as unpaid work, is carried out.

00:01:01.524 --> 00:01:05.776
A custodial sentence is handed down for more serious crimes,

00:01:05.991 --> 00:01:11.203
and for the most serious offences such as murder, it’s a life sentence.